;;
;; REPL/RedTeam/[RT-C]_AdminImpersonation.repl — FAMILY C: admin impersonation.
;;
;; "Can a non-admin reach an admin entrypoint?"
;;
;; This family has a proven precedent in this codebase, which is why it is attacked by EXECUTION
;; rather than by reading: `TS01-A::ORBR|A_Fuel` was written `(with-capability (SECURE) ...)` where
;; that module's `SECURE` is `(defcap SECURE () true)` -- a self-granting cap -- while its own @doc
;; said "can only be used by the Admin". It was verified exploitable by calling it with a non-admin
;; key: it succeeded and billed her 87 IGNIS. Fixed since, but the shape is the point.
;;
;; Run: cd REPL && pact "RedTeam/[RT-C]_AdminImpersonation.repl"
;;
(load "../deploy-stage00.repl")
(load "../deploy-stage01.repl")

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-C-001 - drive eight admin wrappers as a non-admin")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-C-001 · 01 · the P|TS-gated wrappers ====
(print "--- [RT-C-001 · 01 · the P|TS-gated wrappers] ---")
;;<<RT-C-001>> FAMILY: C | STATUS: REFUSED
;;HYPOTHESIS: `TS01-A` carries 30 admin wrappers, and they do NOT gate uniformly. Eleven acquire
;;            `P|ADMINISTRATIVE-SUMMONER`, which composes `GOV|TS01-A_ADMIN` and is a real gate.
;;            FIFTEEN acquire only `P|TS` -- and `(defcap P|TS () true)` grants itself. For those
;;            fifteen the Talos layer contributes NO authorisation at all; the only thing standing
;;            between a stranger and the operation is whatever the CORE function enforces. That is
;;            precisely the shape that made ORBR|A_Fuel exploitable, so it is worth driving rather
;;            than reasoning about.
;;METHOD:     call eight of the fifteen as an ordinary user, chosen for blast radius -- pausing the
;;            chain, moving the OURO source price, flipping gas collection, repricing usage, wiping
;;            treasury debt, setting a branding flag. Record WHICH message refuses each.
;;RESULT:     all eight refused. Seven by an admin-shaped guard, named below. The eighth is
;;            different and is the reason this block is worth more than a row of green ticks.
;;
;;THE RESULT THAT MATTERS IS THE ONE THAT ALMOST PASSED FOR SUCCESS. `DPTF|A_WipeTreasuryDebt` is
;;refused by "Cannot Wipe Positive Treasury Balance" -- a BUSINESS guard, not an authorisation one.
;;Reading `GOV|WIPE_ALL-TREASURY-DEBT` explains why:
;;
;;    (enforce (< treasury-supply 0.0) "Cannot Wipe Positive Treasury Balance")   ;; line 402
;;    (compose-capability (GOV|DPTF_ADMIN))                                       ;; line 403
;;
;;The admin gate IS there, one line below -- but it is UNREACHABLE while the treasury is solvent,
;;which is its normal state. So for this operation the suite can say "a non-admin was refused"
;;without ever having exercised the admin check at all. Had `GOV|DPTF_ADMIN` been missing from that
;;cap, this test would still be green.
;;
;;That is why the assertion below is deliberately worded as the business guard rather than as an
;;admin refusal: writing it as "the admin gate refused" would state something this fixture has not
;;shown. The honest score for this block is SEVEN admin refusals and one shadowed gate, and the
;;shadowed one is logged as a follow-up rather than counted as a pass.
;;
;;A note on why `try` is banned here. An earlier pass ran these eight through `(try "REFUSED" ...)`
;;and reported 8/8 refused -- which is TRUE and useless. The distinction above is invisible without
;;the message, and the shadowed gate would have gone unnoticed.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;--- the six that name DALOS's own admin guard -------------------------------------
            (expect-failure "<<RT-C-001>> a stranger cannot pause the chain"
                "DALOS Admin not satisfed"
                (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_ToggleGAP true))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-C-001>> ...nor flip auto-fueling"
                "DALOS Admin not satisfed"
                (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_SetAutoFueling true))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-C-001>> ...nor toggle account-creation STOA"
                "DALOS Admin not satisfed"
                (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_AccountCreationStoaToggle true))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-C-001>> ...nor switch gas collection on or off"
                "DALOS Admin not satisfed"
                (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_IgnisToggle true true))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-C-001>> ...nor reprice a usage action"
                "DALOS Admin not satisfed"
                (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_UpdateUsagePrice "dptf" 1.0))
            ;;--- one with its own dedicated message ---------------------------------------------
            (expect-failure "<<RT-C-001>> ...nor move the OURO source price that feeds gas economics"
                "Permission not granted to Update OURO Price !"
                (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_SetIgnisSourcePrice 0.5))
            ;;--- one that refuses via a keyset rather than a named message ----------------------
            (expect-failure "<<RT-C-001>> ...nor set a branding flag: BRD answers with its keyset"
                "Keyset failure"
                (ref-TS01-A::BRD|A_SetFlag "OURO-98c486052a51" 1))
            ;;--- the one that WAS shadowed, and is not any more ---------------------------------
            ;;WHEN THIS BLOCK WAS FIRST WRITTEN this assertion read "Cannot Wipe Positive Treasury
            ;;Balance" -- a BUSINESS guard. GOV|DPTF_ADMIN sat one line BELOW a solvency check in
            ;;GOV|WIPE_ALL-TREASURY-DEBT, so a stranger was turned away by the treasury being
            ;;solvent (its normal state) and the admin gate was never reached. The suite could
            ;;report "a non-admin was refused" while the admin check went untested: had
            ;;GOV|DPTF_ADMIN been deleted from that capability, this test would still have passed.
            ;;
            ;;FIXED 2026-09-14 on the owner's ruling -- authorisation precedes business validation,
            ;;swept across all 18 sites in the codebase that had the two in the wrong order. The
            ;;refusal now comes from the admin gate, and the message says so. THE MESSAGE CHANGING
            ;;IS THE PROOF: nothing else about this call changed.
            (expect-failure "<<RT-C-001>> the treasury wipe now refuses on AUTHORISATION, not solvency"
                "DPTF Ownership not verified"
                (ref-TS01-A::DPTF|A_WipeTreasuryDebt))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)
